Appendix A: Detailed Screw Parameters for the 7‑DoF Reference Arm

This appendix provides the complete Product‑of‑Exponentials (POE) parameters for the reference anthropomorphic arm introduced in Chapter 3.5 (Technical Specification). All screw axes are expressed in the global base frame {s} at the home configuration where all joint angles \theta_i = 0. The arm is modelled as a serial chain of seven revolute joints.

A.1 Screw Axis Definition

For a revolute joint, the screw axis \mathcal{S}_i \in \mathbb{R}^6 is defined as

\mathcal{S}_i = \begin{bmatrix} \omega_i \\ v_i \end{bmatrix}, \qquad v_i = -\omega_i \times q_i,

where \omega_i \in \mathbb{R}^3 is the unit direction vector of the joint axis, and q_i \in \mathbb{R}^3 is the coordinate of any point on the axis (both expressed in the base frame at home). The corresponding 4 \times 4 matrix representation is

[\mathcal{S}_i] = \begin{bmatrix} \hat{\omega}_i & v_i \\ 0 & 0 \end{bmatrix} \in \mathfrak{se}(3),

with \hat{\omega}_i the skew‑symmetric matrix of \omega_i.

